{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523363-can-you-use-lashing-out-in-combat","id":1523363,"title":"Can you use lashing out in combat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-09-30T12:20:48-07:00","id":1523363,"title":"Can you use lashing out in combat?","content":"Excerpt below.<br /> <br /> &quot;If the aggressor scores more successes, the victim gains the Condition associated with the aggressor\u2019s Beast. As well, the aggressor gains a +2 die bonus on any rolls to pursue her aspect\u2019s interests for the remainder of the scene.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, could you use the monstrous Beast aspect to gain 2 die on combat rolls and applying the defense penalty that comes from Bestial?<br /> <br /> I see nothing against this use in the text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-30T13:47:19-07:00","id":1523367,"title":"","content":"You can, but note that optimizing for lashing out is pretty difficult, and you have to optimize because if you fail you spent your action giving yourself a penalty. But if you do focus on it, you can get good benefits from it. Make sure to check out the Gangrel Bloodline Onyx Path published, they're all about lashing out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/the-jaws-of-the-beast/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://theo