darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1523363-can-you-use-lashing-out-in-combat?p=1523374#post1523374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's some merits for lashing out in None More Dark's works, and they're high quality works but I probably wouldn't get them just for that. But if you already have them Wild Hunt Gangrel has a merit you probably want if your storyteller will allow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I actually have that book! I liked the passenger/risen beast take on the beast a lot. Thanks again for the help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}